    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on speed-centric upside, with **Corbin Carroll** (81.94) headlining our lineup. Facing the hittable Rocker, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 100% stolen base probability boost due to the starter's slow delivery, compounded by a premium #2 spot in the order. **Mickey Moniak** (75.65) and **James Wood** (69.37) follow closely as high-efficiency anchors; **Mickey Moniak** thrives on a dynamic platoon advantage against Keller, while **James Wood** leverages a favorable #1 lineup position and wind-aided park factors to maximize his run-scoring potential. **Josh Naylor** (74.98) remains our most reliable middle-of-the-order threat, as his matchup against the soft-tossing McCullers Jr. allows him to capitalize on a +19% SP skill adjustment.\n\nThe decision to bench **Kyle Karros** (49.15) was the most difficult call of the morning; he provided a respectable floor, but the optimizer ultimately favored the higher ceiling of **Zach McKinstry** (40.20) despite his lower score, largely due to the defensive necessity of balancing game caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Zach McKinstry**, who faces a sub-4.00 xERA arm and a difficult park factor, placing him right at our threshold. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (54.55) faces a stiff challenge against the lefty Schultz; while the SP xERA is favorable, the -15% dynamic platoon hit keeps his outlook firmly in the \"Marginal\" range. We remain at full strength regarding our core, with **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Jose Caballero** currently sidelined on the IL, leaving no further room for tactical rotation today.",
